  "transcripts": [
    {
      "interviewId": "i01",
      "title": "Rohan Mehta · Full-Stack Badge · raw notes (live call)",
      "notes": "Started 2 min late, camera on, decent setup — VS Code, own project (task manager).\nQ: Walk me through your React project. — Explained component tree clearly, props vs state correct. Lifted state up in the filter without prompting.\nQ: Explain the event loop. — Got the queue/stack idea, used console.log demo. Solid.\nQ: REST error handling. — Froze here. Said 'just try-catch everything' and could not explain status codes (400 vs 401 vs 500 confusion). Recovered partially after hint about semantic codes.\nLive coding: debounce search box. Completed in ~9 min with two hints on the timer cleanup. Would have liked him to test edge case (empty input) unprompted.\nDB: schema for tasks table had no FK to users, called it out, he normalised after discussion.\nOverall: strong React + JS fundamentals, weak HTTP/REST layer, communication clear, owns mistakes. Suggestions were absorbed quickly."
    },
    {
      "interviewId": "i02",
      "title": "Ishita Rao · Full-Stack Badge · raw notes (live call)",
      "notes": "Well prepared, portfolio + deployed project ready.\nQ: Walk me through your app. — Deployed MERN notes app, explained auth flow with JWT refresh, clean.\nQ: Why Next.js over CRA for this? — Gave SSR + SEO reasons, a little surface level but correct.\nLive coding: implement a rate limiter (sliding window). Took ~12 min, needed one hint on memory cleanup of timestamps, then optimised to deque on her own.\nQ: Indexes — when do they hurt? — Knew write penalty, gave the B-tree reason without prompting.\nQ: Git workflow — explained rebase vs merge with a diagram on paper. Nice.\nCon: talked fast, interrupted twice, self-corrected though.\nOverall: interview-ready, breadth and depth both good, minor communication polish needed."
    },
    {
      "interviewId": "i03",
      "title": "Nisha Menon · Data & AI Badge · raw notes (live call)",
      "notes": "Joined from phone first, switched to laptop — started 5 min late.\nQ: Explain your ML project. — Churn prediction, explained feature engineering fine but conflated precision/recall definitions, corrected after I drew the confusion matrix.\nQ: Overfitting — how do you detect and fix? — Knew train/val gap, listed regularisation, dropout, early stopping. Good.\nLive coding: pandas — groupby revenue by month with a rolling mean. Got 80% in 10 min, struggled with .rolling() window param, needed the docs hint.\nQ: SQL — write a join for top-3 customers per region. Window function froze her entirely; knew GROUP BY version only.\nQ: Bias in data — gave the sampling example, thoughtful answer.\nOverall: strong classical ML theory + pandas, SQL window functions and stats rigor below bar. Would not block on personality — coachable, needs one more pass on SQL."
    }
  ],
